# I2 sizing, design D3: numbers slide makers may quote
Simulation and statics only; unbuilt, unvalidated; assumptions in analysis/i2_sizing/report.md section 2.6.
Generated by analysis/i2_sizing/make_report.py from the JSON data through publish.py (rounding policy: report.md, top): loads, resultants, maxima and upper CI bounds are rounded up; capacities, safety factors, envelopes, minima, coverage percentages and lower CI bounds are rounded down; "median" and "p95" are descriptive statistics (nearest). Do not edit by hand.
Paths below are relative to analysis/i2_sizing/. D3 geometry comes from data/d3_contract.json (also read by cad/build_cad_d3.py; checked by test_d3_consistency.py).

1. Force wording (use this everywhere): the passive slip brakes (corner {int:K/T_slip/corner}, lateral {int:K/T_slip/lateral}, centre {int:K/T_slip/centre} N) give >= {int:K/F_lim} N along the fall direction ({cap:R/dyn/passive/280/Fpar_min:1} N minimum over the {ncaught} trials, {cap:S/group_tuned/Fpar_min:0} N minimum over {int:S/group_tuned/n_directions} directions) and <= {int:K/resultant_bound_all_slip} N horizontal resultant ({req:S/group_tuned/Fh_max:1} N); the perpendicular component is up to {req:S/group_tuned/perp_max:0} N (resultant up to {req:S/group_tuned/ang_max:0} deg off the fall). Do not write "<= {int:K/F_lim} N". The resultant is below the static SF-{desc:R/params/SF:1} envelope of {int:K/envelope_SF1p5} N. Source: data/slip.json group_tuned, contract_thresholds.
2. HEADLINE: {int:R/dyn/passive/280/k}/{ncaught} already-caught CP m=0.03 trials (lock {lock28} s, one seeded {ntot}-trial run) arrested within 0.25 m by the passive slip brakes (force per trial = what the brakes give for that trial's fall direction; along-fall component in the 1-D stop, full resultant in the static tip, slide and dynamic tip checks: tip SF >= {desc:R/dyn/passive_params/SF:1}, slide <= {slide_tol_cm} cm, no dynamic tip) = {pctp:280} % (Wilson 95 % CI {ci:R/dyn/passive/280/ci_lo:R/dyn/passive/280/ci_hi} %). Source: data/results.json dyn.passive["280"].
3. Same trials, old metric (fixed {int:K/F_lim} N along the fall, QP tensions): {covf:280}. Source: dyn.passive["280"].fixed300_* and dyn.curves["280|D3 recommended"].
4. Lock-delay sensitivity, passive slip (old fixed-{int:K/F_lim} N in brackets): 0.15 s {covp:150} ({covfs:150}); 0.08 s {covp:080} ({covfs:080}). Source: dyn.passive["150"], ["080"].
5. D0 as proposed, same fixed-{int:K/F_lim} N metric: {covc:280:D0 as proposed:300}. Source: dyn.curves["280|D0 as proposed"].
6. The other {never}/{ntot} trials never engage the catch (unaffected). Falls {falls0}/{ntot} ({falls0_pct} %) become at worst {falls0}+{nfail} = {worst_falls}/{ntot} ({worst_pct} %): a small increase, so never claim fall reduction. Source: dyn.passive["280"].n_fail = {nfail} (old metric: {nfail_fixed}).
7. Static tip SF-{desc:R/params/SF:1} envelope {int:K/envelope_SF1p5} N (SF 1.0: {cap:R/envelope_sf1/D3 recommended/min:0} N); tip SF >= {cap:S/group_tuned/sf_min:2} and sliding SF >= {cap:S/group_tuned/sf_slide_min:2} at the full slip resultant; walker slides at {cap:R/slide_limit/mu=0.5/F_slide:0} N ({cap:R/slide_limit/mu=0.3/F_slide:0} N if mu = 0.3). Denominator for the slip numbers: {int:S/group_tuned/n_directions} motion directions at the nominal pelvis. Source: data/results.json envelope, envelope_sf1, slide_limit; data/slip.json.
8. Required constant force to stop within 0.25 m, {ncaught} caught trials: median {desc:R/loads/280/Freq/median:0} N, p95 {desc:R/loads/280/Freq/p95:0} N (descriptive statistics, nearest; {f491} N is the SPEC damper Dc*v, not a requirement). Source: report.md section 3.
9. COM stopped {desc:R/dyn/passive/280/t_stop/median:3} s after catch engagement (median), p95 {desc:R/dyn/passive/280/t_stop/p95:2} s (descriptive statistics, nearest), {ncaught} trials at lock {lock28} s, passive slip. Source: data/results.json dyn.passive["280"].t_stop.
10. Required hardware: {int:K/mass} kg walker, CG ({geo:K/cg/0:2}, {geo:K/cg/1:0}, {geo:K/cg/2:2}) m, outriggers +{geo:K/outrigger_ex:2} m, mu >= {geo:K/mu_pad:1}, belt half-depth {geo:K/belt/hd:2} / half-width {geo:K/belt/hw:3} m, wheel contacts x = {geo:K/wheels_x/0:3}/{geo:K/wheels_x/1:3}, y = +-{geo:K/wheels_y:3} m, each cable exit point on its contract anchor; rated hold torque {req:S/brake_table_rs0.025/corner/rated_hold_torque:2} / {req:S/brake_table_rs0.025/lateral/rated_hold_torque:2} / {req:S/brake_table_rs0.025/centre/rated_hold_torque:2} N m (corner / lateral / centre). Source: data/d3_contract.json, data/results.json slide_limit.
11. Front-centre anchor: carried by a hinged front gate arm (tube {geo:K/front_gate/tube/width_mm:0} x {geo:K/front_gate/tube/height_mm:0} x {geo:K/front_gate/tube/wall_mm:0} mm {txt:K/front_gate/tube/material}) that latches onto the front-left column; the controller refuses to arm unless the gate is latched. Design cable force {req:G/loads/design_cable_force:1} N, hinge/latch reaction {req:G/latched/hinge_reaction_resultant_N:1} N, peak stress {req:G/latched/sigma_peak_MPa:1} MPa, yield safety factor {cap:G/latched/SF_yield:2}, latch rated >= {req:K/front_gate/design_loads_N/latch_rating_min:1} N. Source: data/gate.json (gate_check.py), section 8b of report.md.
Existing CAD (cad/build_cad.py) is the baseline SEA design, not D3; D3 CAD is cad/build_cad_d3.py.
